# WHAT NEVER GOES INTO THE IMAGE.
#
# The Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .`, so anything not listed here is baked
# into the running container. Before 1.31.0 that included every test file
# — about 350KB of them — because they sat at the project root next to
# the app. They are now under dev/, which is excluded wholesale.
#
# Rule of thumb: if it is not needed to SERVE A REQUEST, it belongs in
# dev/ and therefore never reaches the box.

.git
.gitignore
__pycache__
*.pyc
.venv
venv

# Everything that is not deployed: tests, developer tools, records and
# the AI briefing. See dev/AI-README.md.
dev/

# The long-form human docs. The app does not read them.
README.md

# Runtime state. These live on the NAS in a mounted volume and must never
# be copied in from a build context — a stale database or, far worse, a
# stale session key baked into an image would silently override the real
# one on every deploy.
data/*.db
data/*.db-*
data/settings.json
data/schedule.json
data/secret_key.txt
